description:
Six explicit Unit/Bool interpretations of the reception vocabulary. In the five omission cases, the other four premises hold and SubsistentBeingIsInfiniteReading fails at a being whose esse equals its essence:
- omitting limitation-only-through-reception: one being with limited, unreceived esse that is not infinite;
- omitting reception-only-in-own-essence: esse false received in principle true, which is in potency to it;
- omitting receiver-in-potency: one principle received in itself, with no receptive potency;
- omitting nothing-in-receptive-potency-to-itself: one principle received in, and in potency to, itself;
- omitting unlimited-esse-is-infinite: nothing limited, received or infinite.
A sixth interpretation satisfies all five premises. It has a being whose esse is its essence, and a being whose esse differs from its essence, is received in it, is limited and is not infinite. These are stipulated formal controls only; no metaphysical possibility or rival source reading is claimed.
